Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:01.110 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  for two weeks each year these giant  colorful lanterns float along korea's  namgang river turning it into a  kaleidoscope of light and color  [Applause]  the jinju namgang lantern festival takes  place in jinju south korea annually each  autumn season  [Applause]  a variety of colorful lanterns depicting  national treasures and the cultural  heritage of korea float along the  numgong river and visitors can take boat  rides for a closer look  in addition to the vibrant lanterns  there are live performances of music  fountain displays and of course no  festival is complete without fireworks  the origin of this lantern festival  dates back to the 1500s when the people  of jinju would light lanterns wishing  for the safe return of their family  members during the japanese invasion  today the festival continues in memory  of those soldiers who died serving their  country  visitors to the festival are welcome to  write their own wishes on lanterns and  either hang them in the exhibit tunnel  or float them down the river  [Music]

